{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":33418092,"ns":0,"title":"Cantor tree","extract":"In mathematical set theory, the Cantor tree is either the full binary tree of height ω + 1, or a topological space related to this by joining its points with intervals.\nIt was introduced by Robert Lee Moore in the late 1920s as an example of a non-metrizable Moore space (Jones 1966).","description":"Infinite binary tree","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}